  "hindi": "देवों ने मानव बस्तियों में अग्नि को प्रिय स्थापित किया, मानो बसने को उद्यत मित्र हो। वह उत्सुक रातों में चमके, जो बल के योग्य है, दानी के घर में।",
  "english": "The gods placed Agni as one dear among the human clans, like a friend about to settle. May he shine through the eager nights, he who is worthy of vigour, in the house of the giver.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "dhuḥ is a syncopated perfect (= dadhuḥ) of √dhā. ūrmyā 'night' and the sense of uśatīḥ 'eager' are uncertain; dakṣāyya is uncertain (taken as 'worthy of vigour'); the final ā after dame is left as a separate particle. The comparison 'like a friend about to settle' is the literal reading.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
