  "hindi": "उसकी पुष्टि अपने ही की पुष्टि के समान सुखद है; उस वेग से चलने वाले, दीप्त अग्नि का दर्शन भी। जो औषधियों में अपनी जीभ को धारण करता हुआ, रथ के घोड़े की भाँति पूँछ के बालों को हिलाता है।",
  "english": "His thriving is delightful, as of one's own; the appearance of him, the speeding, blazing one is the same. He who, bearing his tongue among the plants, shakes it about like a chariot horse its tail-hairs.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "dakṣoḥ (read as genitive of dakṣu 'blazing') and hiyānasya 'speeding' are uncertain; saṃdṛṣṭi could also be 'sight' or 'vision'. The simile of the second line (jihvām as object of dodhavīti, vārān compared) is rendered literally; the exact syntax is unclear. In the translations the possessor 'his' is Agni, understood from the hymn; the verse itself does not name him.",
